rd order, then in reverse order. Copy all cell values unchanged; only the layout changes. Validate dimensions, each row's reversed-left/original-right halves, and the three band orderings against demonstrations.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:28:18.001Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:28:18.001Z","version":1},"after":{"id":"arc_three_band_horizontal_mirror_tiling","kind":"memory","title":"Expand ARC grids into three vertically stacked, horizontally mirrored bands","content":"For this demonstrated ARC task family, transform an input grid of height H and width W into a 3H×2W output. The vertical source-row sequence is the input rows in reverse order, then the input rows in original order, then the input rows in reverse order again. For each source row, construct its output row by concatenating the row reversed horizontally with the original row. Preserve every source cell value unchanged. The 3×13→9×26 demonstration validates this exact ordering. Validate output dimensions, row sequence, horizontal concatenation, and copied values.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:28:18.001Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:30:18.874Z","version":2},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682263/attempts/f584a00acdda4d60937d1e953c54734b/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
