{"id":"refine_20260929125445886","summary":"Updated the global ARC motif-stamping memory with the demonstrated rule for copying a multicolor motif onto isolated target markers.","rationale":"In task-8ceb4c33, a 5×3 motif and two isolated zero markers established center-anchor stamping; the test used a 5×1 motif and color-8 markers, and the same rule solved it correctly.","expectedOutcome":"Future motif-stamping solutions should recognize isolated target markers, align each with the motif's center anchor, preserve the motif's cell arrangement, and validate that each translated copy fits while leaving the source unchanged.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"infer_motif_stamping_from_arc_demonstrations","title":"Infer motif stamping from ARC demonstrations","content":"For ARC grids containing a compact non-background multicolor motif and isolated target markers, infer the motif's exact colored-cell offsets from its geometric center anchor. When demonstrations support it, stamp a copy at every target marker by aligning the motif's center anchor to that marker; replace the marker with the motif's anchor color and preserve the motif's cell arrangement. Keep the original motif and background unchanged. Check that each translated copy fits within the grid and that the stamped cells match the inferred motif. This was validated in task-8ceb4c33: a 5×3 motif with center color 3 was stamped at two zero markers, and a 5×1 motif [7,1,7,7,7] with center color 1 was stamped at every color-8 marker.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Adds a demonstrated center-anchor stamping variant to the existing reusable ARC motif-stamping memory.","before":{"id":"infer_motif_stamping_from_arc_demonstrations","kind":"memory","title":"Infer motif stamping from ARC demonstrations","content":"For noisy ARC grids, identify the rare non-background seed color and record the exact coordinates of its colored cells as offsets from an anchor. Scan every in-bounds translation in the same fixed orientation. A translation matches when every footprint offset lands on a target-background zero cell; unoccupied cells inside the footprint's bounding box do not constrain the match. Recolor the matched footprint cells to the seed color, taking the union if matches overlap. Preserve all other cells, including noise, nonzero background, and the original seed. Infer the target condition and colors from demonstrations rather than assuming them. Validated across examples with seed colors 2, 4, and 8, including a 3-cell L footprint; verify by checking all candidate placements and that only matching footprint cells change.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:45:17.668Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:02:55.620Z","version":4},"after":{"id":"infer_motif_stamping_from_arc_demonstrations","kind":"memory","title":"Infer motif stamping from ARC demonstrations","content":"For ARC grids containing a compact non-background multicolor motif and isolated target markers, infer the motif's exact colored-cell offsets from its geometric center anchor. When demonstrations support it, stamp a copy at every target marker by aligning the motif's center anchor to that marker; replace the marker with the motif's anchor color and preserve the motif's cell arrangement. Keep the original motif and background unchanged. Check that each translated copy fits within the grid and that the stamped cells match the inferred motif. This was validated in task-8ceb4c33: a 5×3 motif with center color 3 was stamped at two zero markers, and a 5×1 motif [7,1,7,7,7] with center color 1 was stamped at every color-8 marker.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:45:17.668Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:54:52.717Z","version":5},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baseli