{"id":"refine_20260929134903653","summary":"Updated the global task-b41a3464 memory with a correctly validated horizontal-separator instance.","rationale":"The trajectory confirms the existing separator-comparison rule for both vertical and horizontal separators: align the panels without flipping and mark equal cells with 3, otherwise 2.","expectedOutcome":"Future solutions can handle either separator orientation and validate the output dimensions against the panel dimensions and each output cell against the aligned input pair.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"arc_separator_comparison_mark_equal_cells","title":"ARC separator comparison: mark equal cells","content":"For ARC task-b41a3464-style inputs, split the grid at the full-height vertical or full-width horizontal solid separator. Remove the separator, align the two equal-sized panels at corresponding coordinates without flipping either panel, and output one cell per aligned pair: use color 3 when the input colors are equal and color 2 otherwise. Validated with a vertical separator producing a 21×8 output and a horizontal separator in a 21×13 input (separator row 10) producing a 10×13 output. Check panel dimensions, separator removal, and each cellwise comparison.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Adds a correctly solved horizontal-separator instance and confirms the rule applies to either separator orientation.","before":{"id":"arc_separator_comparison_mark_equal_cells","kind":"memory","title":"ARC separator comparison: mark equal cells","content":"For ARC task-b41a3464, the input contains two equal-sized grids separated by a solid line (separator can be vertical or horizontal). Split the grids at the separator and compare corresponding coordinates without flipping either half. The output has the dimensions of one half. Put color 3 wherever the two corresponding input cells are equal; put the shared background color elsewhere. Demonstrations used two different foreground colors an